{"id": "9bce2436-6348-4720-b747-e733fac39f6b", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T12:33:14.823571", "source": "user", "parent_id": "ad85165a-1d27-44ad-a3d1-b503164356e8", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Bhai, kaam shuru karne se pehle sirf inspection aur plan chahiye — full design abhi mat bhejo.\\n\\nPlease do and return ONLY the following:\\n\\n1) Inspection pass (no implementation, no experiments):\\n   - List what is actually present in /workspace (QuaRot repo? LLaMA-2 weights or only HF config? benchmark/eval harness? CUDA kernels? quantization calibration data?).\\n   - State clearly which of these are absent, given network is disabled and GPU is disabled in this environment.\\n   - Confirm the runtime/python situation (system Python, project deps not preinstalled).\\n\\n2) Proposed approach outline (short, 8-15 bullets max):\\n   - What comparison arms you would define (e.g., FP16/BF16 baseline vs QuaRot W4A4 prefill vs decode), which LLaMA-2 sizes, which sequence lengths and batch sizes.\\n   - Which metrics you would measure separately for prefill vs decode (latency, throughput tokens/s, TTFT, memory footprint, perplexity/quality drop) and how you would separate compute-bound prefill from memory-bound decode.\\n   - What the main confounds look like (kernel maturity, fused rotation application, online Hadamard cost, KV-cache quantization) and how the design would isolate them.\\n\\n3) Consequential assumptions and open uncertainties only:\\n   - Which model sizes/precision baselines are assumed, what hardware the design targets, what counts as the quality metric.\\n   - Anything the repo does not actually tell you.\\n\\nDo not fabricate hardware, dataset, or runtime numbers. If something cannot be inspected because it is missing, say so and mark it as an assumption in the design. Keep it concise and concrete; I will review the approach before asking for the full deliverable.\", \"