00 70B) should be used as an anchor/reference arm — needs your decision.\n\n**Questions I would want answered before the full design** (pick any; I will default otherwise): (a) which GPU, (b) include 70B or cap at 13B, (c) is quality purely perplexity or also zero-shot accuracy, (d) batch-1 latency or large-batch throughput as the headline metric, (e) is comparing against published QuaRot paper numbers in scope, (f) is a CPU-only analytic/roofline dry run useful as the sandbox-executable portion of the deliverable?", "evidence": "All statements in section 1 come from direct execution in the sandbox: `ls -la /workspace` → only task.json (405 B), `du -sh /workspace` → 8.0K; `cat /workspace/task.json` → contains \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\"; `find / -maxdepth 4 -iname '*quarot*'` → empty; `~/.cache` absent, no HF cache, no /opt, no *.whl, no libtorch; python 3.14.4 at /usr/bin/python3, pip 25.1.1, and a `find_spec` probe showing torch/transformers/numpy/datasets/accelerate/sentencepiece/tokenizers/scipy/pandas/triton/lm_eval all False; `nvidia-smi` → \"couldn't communicate with the NVIDIA driver\", no /dev/nvidia* nodes (only a libcuda.so.595.71.05 userspace stub and a CUDA 13.1 toolkit tree with no bound device); `nproc`=224, MemTotal ≈ 2.1 TB, Xeon Platinum 8570, gcc-15 + git available, /tmp tmpfs 1 TB; network probes to pypi.org and `git ls-remote github.com/spcl/QuaRot` both failed with DNS resolution errors, so repo/weights/datasets cannot be obtained. Nothing about LLaMA sizes, layer shapes, or QuaRot kernel internals was observed locally — those are flagged as assumptions. No command produced any performance or perplexity number, and none is reported.", "assumptions": ["Hardware target is a datacenter GPU not present in this sandbox (A100-80GB assumed primary, H100 alternative); 70B assumed to require two such GPUs.", "LLaMA-2 7B/13B are the primary models and 70B is optional; BF16 (FP16-equivalent) is the baseline precision a