metic intensity). Explicitly **no** latency or PPL numbers produced here.\\n\\n## 3) Consequential assumptions & open uncertainties\\n\\n**Assumptions (not fixed by the task or the environment):**\\n- Hardware target is a single datacenter GPU (A100-80GB assumed, H100 as alternative); 70B assumed to need 2 GPUs. The sandbox has none of this.\\n- LLaMA-2 7B/13B(/70B), BF16 as the precision baseline (FP16 treated as equivalent); FP16-vs-FP16-with-kernel-overhead is the intended reference.\\n- Quality = WikiText-2/C4 perplexity with \\u0394PPL threshold \\u2248 0.1\\u20130.25 for \\\"acceptable\\\"; speed = latency at B=1 and throughput at B\\u22658.\\n- A QuaRot-style implementation with custom INT4 GEMM + online Hadamard kernels and offline weight folding is available somewhere outside this sandbox.\\n- OpenAI-style C4 calibration subset (128\\u00d72048) is used for scale-fitting; scale search is offline and excluded from all latency timing.\\n\\n**Open uncertainties / things the repository does NOT tell us (because there is no repository here):**\\n- Whether QuaRot's INT4 GEMM actually beats FP16 at large-batch prefill on the target GPU \\u2014 this is a *result*, and the sign is genuinely uncertain (that is why the design measures both regimes rather than assuming a uniform speedup).\\n- Whether the online Hadamard overhead erases the W4A4 gain at long context, and where the crossover S is.\\n- Whether 4-bit KV hurts quality more at 70B than at 7B (paper-reported trends are not re-verifiable here).\\n- Actual kernel/harness details, flag names, whether `R1/R2/R3/R4` rotations and online Hadamards are fused in the shipped code, and what calibration settings the official repo uses \\u2014 all unverifiable without the source; they become parameterized placeholders in the design rather than facts.\\n- Whether the published QuaRot latency table (single-A100 7B, 2-A100 70B) should be used as an anchor/reference arm \\u2014 needs your decision.\\n\\n**Questions I would wa