xt-2 and C4 perplexity with an acceptability threshold of roughly 0.1-0.25 delta PPL; zero-shot accuracy is secondary.\", \"A QuaRot-style implementation with custom INT4 GEMM plus online Hadamard kernels and offline weight folding exists outside this sandbox; its actual code layout, flags and fusion behavior are unverifiable here.\", \"Calibration uses an OpenAI-style C4 subset (128 sequences x 2048 tokens) and all scale-fitting is offline, excluded from timing.\", \"Prefill is treated as compute-bound at S>=1024 and batch>=8, decode as memory-bandwidth-bound at batch 1; this is a hypothesis the design tests, not a given.\", \"Published QuaRot paper numbers may be used as a reference arm only if the researcher approves; they are not treated as measurements of this experiment.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Whether QuaRot's INT4 GEMM actually exceeds FP16 throughput at large-batch prefill on the target GPU; the sign of the prefill speedup is genuinely unknown and is a measured outcome, not a premise.\", \"The sequence-length crossover at which online Hadamard overhead offsets the 4-bit gain (if one exists).\", \"Whether 4-bit KV-cache quantization degrades quality more at 70B than at 7B.\", \"Kernel maturity and fusion state of the shipped QuaRot code (R1-R4 folding, fused vs unfused online Hadamard), and its exact calibration settings - unresolvable without the repository.\", \"Whether the INT4 tensor-core path exists on the chosen GPU (A100 yes, H100 no), which changes the prefill interpretation entirely.\", \"Whether the intended baseline should be a locally re-run BF16 harness, the paper's published table, or both.\", \"No part of this environment can execute the measurement, so feasibility of the full design depends entirely on resources outside the sandbox.\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-ff36a26a-77dd-9be6-9f02-7916ed84e6c9", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "end_researcher_turn: {\"stage\": \"plan\", \"answer\": \"## 1) Inspection pass (facts, not inference)\\n\\n**/workspace contents \\u2014 effectively empty:**\\n- `/workspace/task.json` (405 B) only. Whole tree is 8 KB. `documents.track.md` field inside task.json says: *\\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"*\\n- **No QuaRot repo** (searched `/` for `*quarot*` at depth 4 \\u2192 nothing; no git checkout anywhere).\\n- **No LLaMA-2 weights, no HF config, no tokenizer** \\u2014 no HF hub cache (`~/.cache` does not exist), no `/opt`, no safetensors/bin anywhere.\\n- **No benchmark or eval harness** (no lm_eval, no harness scripts).\\n- **No QuaRot CUDA kernels** (no Machete/CUTLASS/online-Hadamard sources; nothing to build).\\n- **No quantization calibration data** (no C4/WikiText-2 copies, `datasets: []`).\\n- Network is genuinely dead: DNS resolution fails for both pypi.org and github.com (tested), so none of the above can be fetched.\\n- **Runtime:** system `python3` = 3.14.4 at `/usr/bin/python3`; pip 25.1.1 exists but **zero project deps installed** \\u2014 `torch, transformers, numpy, datasets, accelerate, sentencepiece, tokenizers, scipy, pandas, triton` all report `False`. Python 3.14 is also newer than what the real QuaRot stack (torch ~2.2\\u20132.4) ships wheels for, so even with network a venv plan would be needed.\\n- **Compute:** `gpu_enabled=false` confirmed \\u2014 `nvidia-smi` cannot reach the driver, no `/dev/nvidia*` nodes (a `libcuda.so.595.71.05` user stub and a CUDA 13.1 toolkit under `/usr/local/cuda-13.1` exist, but there is no device to run on). CPU-only host: 224 usable cores (`cpu_affinity_count=224`), Xeon Platinum 8570, ~2 TB RAM, gcc-15/git/cmake-less toolchain, `/tmp` tmpfs 1 TB.\\n\\n**Verdict:** the \\\"end-to-end 4-bit vs FP16\\\" performance question cannot be *measured* here. This is a design-only deliverable; every number below is a to-be-measured quantity, none is invented.\\n\\n## 2) Proposed approach outline\\n\\n- **Arms (all on the same serving harness to keep kernel maturity constant):** A0 = BF16/FP16 baseline; A1 = W4A16 weight-only (AWQ-style) as the \\\"cheap quantization\\\" reference point; A2 = QuaRot W4A4 with 16-bit KV; **A3 = QuaRot W4A4 + 4-bit KV (the paper's full config)**; A4 = A3 minus online Hadamard on `down_proj`; A5 = A3 minus KV Hadamard/quant (KV16); A6 = A3 with offline-rotations-only (no online transforms, naive \\u2192 shows why they exist); A7 = W8A8 INT as an upper-bound sanity ceiling.\\n- **Models:** LLaMA-2 **7B and 13B primary, 70B secondary** (70B only if \\u22652\\u00d780 GB GPUs exist; otherwise dropped, stated up front).\\n- **Shapes:** prefill `S \\u2208 {128, 512, 1024, 2048, 4096}` \\u00d7 `batch \\u2208 {1, 8, 32, 64}`; decode measured at prompt 128 with output length 128/512, batch {1,8,32,64}; plus one long-context ladder (up to 32k) *only* for the online-Hadamard-cost arm.\\n- **Prefill metrics:** TTFT (= prefill latency), prefill tokens/s, effective TFLOP/s and % of peak INT4/FP16, prefill memory high-water, per-op split (GEMM vs rotate vs quantize) from the profiler.\\n- **Decode metrics:** per-token latency at batch 1 (ms/token), aggregate tokens/s at batch B, end-to-end footprint = weights + KV cache (GB, and the theoretical KV bytes/token as a covariate), plus bytes-moved/token so the memory-bound prediction can be tested rather than assumed.\\n- **Regime separation (the core of the question):** report **speedup vs arithmetic intensity**, not two scalars \\u2014 prefill at S\\u22651024, B\\u22658 is compute-bound (tests whether INT4 GEMM throughput + Hadamard overhead nets out), decode at B=1 is bandwidth-bound (tests whether weight/KV byte compression pays off). One matched-shape microbenchmark (INT4 GEMM vs FP16 GEMM at exactly the model's layer shapes) attributes any prefill shortfall to *kernel efficiency* rather than to the quantization scheme.\\n- **Quality metric (kept separate from speed):** WikiText-2 PPL (len-512, GPTQ/QuaRot convention) + C4 PPL as primary, \\u0394 vs BF16; secondary zero-shot battery (e.g. PiQA/ARC-E/HellaSwag/WinoGrande) to catch PPL-insensitive damage. A3 is a \\\"win\\\" only if it hits the speed target at \\u0394PPL \\u2264 a pre-registered threshold.\\n- **Confound 1 \\u2014 kernel maturity:** identical backend for FP16 and INT4 paths where possible; matched-shape GEMM microbench as the control; never compare QuaRot's custom kernel against a different team's FP16 kernel unbenchmarked.\\n- **Confound 2 \\u2014 fused vs unfused rotation:** toggle fusion + block size and report online-Hadamard time as % of step time, so a regression is attributed to plumbing, not to 4-bit math.\\n- **Confound 3 \\u2014 online Hadamard scaling:** its cost grows with sequence length (log-linear in S); hence the long-context ladder, reported as *marginal* cost vs S rather than folded into one average.\\n- **Confound 4 \\u2014 KV-cache quantization entangled with attention path:** A3 vs A5 isolates the KV-quant decision from activation-quant; A3 vs A2 isolates KV-Hadamard.\\n- **Confound 5 \\u2014 calibration/rotation randomness:** \\u22653 calibration seeds + \\u22653 random-rotation seeds; rotation *type* (random Hadamard vs Hadamard-designated for online transforms) held fixed within a comparison.\\n- **Confound 6 \\u2014 hardware ISA:** A100 has INT4 tensor cores, H100 does not (INT8 pairs) \\u2014 hardware must be pinned before interpreting prefill numbers.\\n- **Measurement protocol:** locked clocks, \\u226510 warmup + 20 timed iters, report **median + IQR**, CUDA-graph/`torch.compile` state identical across arms, one process per arm, results dumped as per-run CSV.\\n- **Deliverable given this sandbox:** a runnable-experiment *spec* (config matrix + harness skeleton + analysis script), plus a CPU-feasible dry run of the non-GPU parts only (model-config-derived FLOP/byte accounting and the roofline/regime-map plot from analytic arithmetic intensity). Explicitly **no** latency or PPL numbers produced here.\\n\\n## 3) Consequential assumptions & open uncertainties\\n\\n**Assumptions (not fixed by the task or the environment):**\\n- Hardware target is a single datacenter GPU (A100-80GB assumed, H100 as alternative); 70B assumed to need 2 GPUs. The sandbox has none of this.\\n- LLaMA-2 7B/13B(/70B), BF16 as the precision baseline (FP16 treated as equivalent); FP16-vs-FP16-with-kernel-overhead is the intended reference.\\n- Quality = WikiText-2/C4 perplexity with \\u0394PPL threshold \\u2248 0.1\\u20130.25 for \\\"acceptable\\\"; speed = latency at B=1 and throughput at B\\u22658.\\n- A QuaRot-style implementation with custom INT4 GEMM + online Hadamard kernels and offline weight folding is available somewhere outside this sandbox.\\n- OpenAI-style C4 calibration subset (128\\u00d72048) is used for scale-fitting; scale search is offline and excluded from all latency timing.\\n\\n**Open uncertainties / things the repository does NOT tell us (because there is no repository here):**\\n- Whether QuaRot's INT4 GEMM actually beats FP16 at large-batch prefill on the target GPU \\u2014 this is a *result*, and the sign is genuinely uncertain (that is why the design measures both regimes rather than assuming a uniform speedup).\\n- Whether the online Hadamard overhead erases the W4A4 gain at long context, and where the crossover S is.\\n- Whether 4-bit KV hurts quality more at 70B than at 7B (paper-reported trends are not re-verifiable here).\\n- Actual kernel/harness details, flag names, whether `R1/R2/R3/R4` rotations and online Hadamards are fused in the shipped code, and what calibration settings the official repo uses \\u2014 all unverifiable without the source; they become parameterized placeholders in the design rather than facts.\\n- Whether the published QuaRot latency table (single-A100 7B, 2-A100 70B) should be used as an anchor/reference arm \\u2014 needs your decision.\\n\\n**Questions I would want answered before the full design** (pick any; I will default otherwise): (a) which GPU, (b) include 70B or cap at 13B, (c) is quality purely perplexity or also zero-shot accuracy, (d) batch-1 latency or large-batch throughput as the headline metric, (e) is comparing against published QuaRot paper numbers in scope, (f) is a CPU-only analytic/roofline dry run useful as the sandbox-executable portion of the deliverable?\", \"evidence\": \"All statements in section 1 come from direct execution in the sandbox: `ls -la /workspace` \\u2192 only task.json (405 B), `du -sh /workspace` \\u2192 8.0K; `cat /workspace/task.json` \\u2192 contains \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"; `find / -maxdepth 4 -iname '*quarot*'` \\u2192 empty; `~/.cache` absent, no HF cache, no /opt, no *.whl, no libtorch; python 3.14.4 at /usr/bin/python3, pip 25.1.1, and a `find_spec` probe showing torch/transformers/numpy/datasets/accelerate/sentencepiece/tokenizers/scipy/pandas/triton/lm_eval all False; `nvidia-smi` \\u2192 \\\"couldn't communicate with the NVIDIA driver\\\", no /dev/nvidia* nodes (only a libcuda.so.595.71.05 userspace stub and a CUDA 13.1 toolkit tree with no bound device); `nproc`=224, MemTotal \\u2248 2.1 TB, Xeon Platinum 8570, gcc-15 + git available, /tmp tmpfs 1 TB; network probes to pypi.org and `git ls-remote github.com/spcl/QuaRot` both failed with DNS resolution errors, so repo/weights/datasets cannot be obtained. Nothing about LLaMA sizes, layer shapes, or QuaRot kernel internals was observed locally \\u2014 those are flagged as assumptions. No command produced any performance or perplexity number, and none is reported.\", \"assumptions\": [\"Hardware target is a datacenter GPU not present in this sandbox (A100-80GB assumed primary, H100 alternative); 70B assumed to require two such GPUs.\", \"LLaMA-2 7B/13B are the primary models and 70B is optional; BF16 (FP16-equivalent) is the baseline precision arm.\", \"Quality is measured by WikiText-2 and C4 perplexity with an acceptability threshold of roughly 0.1-0.25 delta PPL; zero-shot accuracy is secondary.\", \"A QuaRot-style implementation with custom INT4 GEMM plus online Hadamard kernels and offline weight folding exists outside this sandbox; its actual code layout, flags and fusion behavior are unverifiable here.\", \"Calibration uses an OpenAI-style C4 subset (128 sequences x 2048 tokens) and all scale-fitting is offline, excluded from timing.\", \"Prefill is treated as compute-bound at S>=1024 and batch>=8, decode as memory-bandwidth-bound at batch 1; this is a hypothesis the design tests, not a given.\", \"Published QuaRot paper numbers may be used as a reference arm only if the researcher approves; they are not treated as measurements of this experiment.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Whether QuaRot's INT4 GEMM actually exceeds FP16 throughput at large-batch prefill on the target GPU; the sign of the prefill speedup is genuinely unknown and is a measured outcome, not a premise.\", \"The sequence-length crossover at which online Hadamard overhead offsets the 4-bit gain (if one exists).\", \"Whether 4-bit KV-cache quantization degrades quality more at 70B than at 7B.\", \"Kernel maturity and fusion state of the shipped QuaRot code (R1-R4 folding, fused vs unfused online Hadamard), and its exact calibration settings - unresolvable without the repository.\", \"Whether the INT4 tensor-core path exists on the chosen GPU (A100 yes, H100 no), which changes the prefill interpretation entirely.\", \"Whether the intended baseline should be a locally re-run BF16 harness, the paper's published table, or both.\", \"No part of this environment can execute the measurement, so feasibility of the full design depends entirely on resources outside the sandbox.\"]}", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
