{"id": "b82b5163-5980-4237-91cc-fdcb94e1e692", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T12:36:54.797680", "source": "user", "parent_id": "1694111a-2d65-48ba-b077-a527e4de0ec8", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Bhai, inspection clean hai aur approach mujhe sahi lagti hai. Main approve kar raha hoon. Aapke (a)-(f) defaults yeh rahe — inhe design mein fixed maano:\\n\\n(a) GPU: primary A100-80GB (single GPU for 7B/13B), H100 ko explicitly ek \\\"no-INT4-TC\\\" alternative condition ke roop mein parameterize karo — prefill interpretation hardware-pinned rahe.\\n(b) Scope: 7B + 13B primary; 70B optional/secondary arm, conditional on >=2x80GB, aur budget-exceed hone par cleanly drop ho jaye (drop criteria pehle se likho).\\n(c) Quality: perplexity primary (WikiText-2 len-512 + C4), zero-shot battery secondary/diagnostic. Pre-registered ΔPPL acceptance band rakho (aapka 0.1-0.25 theek hai) aur usse \\\"quality-neutral\\\" ka operational definition banao.\\n(d) Headline metric: do regimes ke speedups — decode = batch-1 per-token latency, prefill = large-batch (S>=1024, B>=8) tokens/s + TTFT. Ek scalar \\\"average speedup\\\" mat dena.\\n(e) Published QuaRot numbers: sirf sanity reference anchor ke roop mein, alag table mein, never mixed into your own CIs; clearly label ki woh externally reported hain.\\n(f) CPU-only analytic dry run: haan, include karo — lekin sirf non-GPU arithmetic (FLOP/byte accounting, arithmetic-intensity/roofline regime map, predicted bytes-moved/token aur KV-bytes/token curves). Isse koi measured latency ya PPL claim mat karna.\\n\\nDo refinements jo design mein zaroor chahiye:\\n1. Arms ka ordering/causal attribution explicit ho: har ablation (A4 no online Hadamard on down_proj, A5 no KV-quant, A6 offline-rotations-only, A1 W4A16, A7 W8A8) ek specific hypothesis ko test kare, aur prefill vs decode par uska expected direction pehle se likha ho — taaki result aane par \\\"kaunsa component kis regime mein cost/benefit de raha hai\\\" ka attribution possible ho.\\n2. Confound handling measurable banayein: (i) matched-shape INT4-vs-FP16 GEMM microbenchmark ko first-class control banao (kernel efficiency vs quantization scheme separation), (ii) online-Hadamard marginal cost vs S ko long-context ladder par report karo, mean mein fold mat karo, (iii) fused/unfused toggle aur calibration/rotation seeds (>=3 each) protocol mein fixed karo, (iv) CUDA-graph/compile state aur clock-locking across arms identical.\\n\\nSath hi, analysis plan mein explicit decision rule rakho: kaunsi condition par aap design \\\"W4A4 helps decode but not prefill\\\" jaisa conclusion claim karoge, aur kaunsi observation ko \\\"kernel immaturity\\\" ke roop mein attribute karke scheme se alag karenge.\\n\\nAb poora deliverable bhejo: rationale, control structure (arms + ablations + controls + seeds), config matrix, measurement protocol, analysis plan (regime/speedup-vs-arithmetic-intensity framing, ΔPPL gates, attribution rules), resources/runtime estimate with assumptions clearly marked, risks/limitations, aur CPU-feasible dry-run portion ka scope. Koi bhi latency/throughput/PPL number mat do — sab placeholder ya analytic hi hona chahiye. Jo bhi repo/hardware fact verify nahi ho sakta, usse assumption flag karo.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"result\", \"approach_approved\": true}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
{"id": "d35c4912-1dce-432c-b83b-55f0947218fb", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T12:38:24.733689", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "b82b5163-5980-4237-91cc-fdcb94e1e692", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": "The researcher approved and wants the full design. Let me do a bit more CPU-feasible analytic dry-run work to ground the arithmetic accounting (FLOP/byte accounting, arithmetic intensity, KV bytes/token curves) — that's allowed and adds real value as an analytic artifact. I can compute model config-derived numbers (LLaMA-2 7B/13B/70B dims — these are public architectural constants, but I should flag them as assumed-from-public-config since no HF config exists locally).\n\nLet me write a small script in /tmp that computes:\n- weights bytes per arm (W4A16 → ~0.5x + scales overhead, W4A4, W8A8, FP16)\n- KV bytes/token per model per precision\n- arithmetic intensity per token for decode (memory-bound) and per token for prefill (FLOPs / bytes)\n- arithmetic intensity of GEMM layers as function of batch/seq → regime map classification\n- predicted speedup bounds from roofline: for decode, speedup ≤ weight-bytes ratio (bandwidth-bound); for prefill, speedup ≤ peak-FLOPS ratio × kernel efficiency\n- crossover batch size / sequence length where a layer transitions from memory- to compute-bound given assumed peak FLOPS and bandwidth (A100 80GB: 312 TFLOPS FP16, ~1555 TFLOPS INT8, INT4 nominally 624; bandwidth 2.0 TB/s HBM2e; H100: 990 TFLOPS FP16, ~1979 INT8, no INT4 TC, 3.35 TB/s). These are hardware spec constants — I must flag them as external spec values, not measurements, and treat them as parameters. That's fine — they're datasheet parameters, not experiment outcomes. I'll mark clearly.\n\nLet me build the analytic table. Also compute the predicted bytes-moved/token curves vs context length and the online-Hadamard FLOP cost O(S log S) per KV head as a fraction of attention FLOPs.\n\nLet me be careful to present these as analytic predictions with formulas, not measured.\n\nLet me write the script.\n\nModel configs (public, assumed):\n- LLaMA-2 7B: h=4096, L=32, heads=32, kv_heads=32 (MHA, no GQA), intermediate=11008, vocab=32000\n- LLaMA-2 13B: h=5120, L=40, heads=40, kv=40, inter=13824, vocab=32000\n- LLaMA-2 70B: h=8192, L=80, heads=64, kv=8 (GQA), inter=28672, vocab=32000\n\nParameters: non-embedding ≈ 12*L*h^2 + 8*L*h^2? Let's compute: attention qkv+o = 4h^2; MLP (up, gate, down) = 3*h*inter; per layer 4h^2 + 3*h*inter. Embedding = vocab*h (tied in LLaMA-2).\n\nKV bytes/token = 2 (K and V) * L * h * bytes_per_elem. For 70B: 2 * L * (kv_heads * head_dim=8*128=1024).\n\nLet me compute quickly with python.\n\nAlso compute arithmetic intensity per layer type:\n- GEMM with batch M tokens: FLOPs = 2*M*h*out, bytes = h*out*bytes_w + M*h*bytes_a + M*out*bytes_a. For decode M=B (small) → weight-dominated → AI ≈ 2*B/bytes_w. For prefill M=B*S large → activation-dominated → AI ≈ 2/ (2*bytes_a) ... roughly h*out dominates weights when M small.\n\nRoofline crossover M* = (bytes per weight element ratio) — the key: memory-bound iff AI < peak_flops/bandwidth. For A100 FP16: 312e12/2.035e12 ≈ 153 FLOP/byte. INT8: 624e12/2.035e12 ≈ 307. So decode at B=1 with FP16 weights AI ≈ 2*1/2 = 1 FLOP/byte → deeply memory bound (153x margin). Prefill at M=8192 tokens FP16 AI ≈ 2*8192/(...)? Let's compute properly.\n\nThe crossover batch/seq where layer becomes compute-bound: for FP16 weights (2 bytes/elem), AI ≈ 2M/(2 + small) → memory-bound when 2M/2 < 153 → M < 153 tokens. So prefill with M≥1024 tokens is compute-bound. That's a nice analytic justification of regime separation. For INT4 weights (0.5 bytes + scale overhead ~ 0.5 + 2/128 ≈ 0.516), crossover at M ≈ peak_int4/BW/2... For A100 INT4 (624 TFLOPS): 624/2.035 = 307 FLOP/byte; AI = 2M/0.516 → M* ≈ 79? Hmm wait, that means INT4 becomes compute-bound earlier at smaller M... Actually crossover M* = (peak/BW)*bytes_w/2 = 307*0.516/2 ≈ 79 tokens. And FP16 M* = 153*2/2 = 153 tokens. So both are compute-bound in prefill at M≥1024; the theoretical speedup in compute-bound regime = peak_int4/peak_fp16 = 2x, in memory-bound regime = bytes ratio = 2/0.516 ≈ 3.9x. These are analytic upper bounds (ignoring quant/rotation overhead and kernel efficiency). Great — that's exactly the kind of analytic prediction that's allowed and useful for the regime map.\n\nAlso decode KV-dominated: at long context, bytes moved = weights + S*KV_bytes_per_token; so decode speedup shrinks as S grows because KV dominates and 4-bit KV only gives 4x on KV vs 16-bit baseline... Actually baseline KV is FP16, QuaRot KV is 4-bit → KV bytes ratio 4x too. But at 70B with GQA, KV/token = 2*80*1024*2 = 327,680 bytes = 320KB/token for FP16. Weight bytes for 70B FP16 ≈ 140 GB. So KV would need S ≈ 140GB/0.32MB ≈ 437k tokens to dominate — but batch: with B=64, KV total = B*S. At B=1, S=4096 → 1.3 GB vs 140 GB weights. So decode at B=1 is weight-dominated until absurd context. At 7B: weights FP16 13.5 GB, KV/token FP16 = 2*32*4096*2 = 524 KB; S=4096 → 2.1 GB (15%). So KV matters somewhat at 7B. Good analytic nuance.\n\nOnline Hadamard cost: for KV cache Hadamard on the value/output activations of size h: cost = h log2 h FLOPs per token per application; relative to attention+MLP FLOPs per token (~2*(4h^2 + 3h*inter)) — tiny per token in decode; but the KV-cache Hadamard applied to the *whole* cache periodically is O(S h log h) per layer per call → grows linearly with S. Also the online Hadamard for down_proj input is per token: activation width inter, so inter*log2(inter) FLOPs vs down_proj GEMM 2*inter*h. For 7B: 11008*13.4 = 147k vs 2*11008*4096=90M → 0.16% FLOPs, but it's bandwidth-bound (read activation, write rotated activation = 2*inter*bytes) which matters in decode. That's a nice analytic insight: online Hadamard is a bandwidth/latency overhead not a FLOP overhead → expected to hurt decode more than prefill in FLOP terms, but its cost is fixed per token whereas... hmm. In decode, per-layer extra traffic = 2*inter*2 bytes = 44 KB (FP16 activation) vs layer weights 4h²*... For 7B MLP weights per layer ≈ 3*4096*11008*2 bytes = 270 MB. So 0.016% — negligible. But kernel launch overhead + non-fused extra passes (4 extra kernels per layer × 32 layers) is what actually hurts. That is exactly a confound the design must isolate — good, and it's not measurable analytically → flag.\n\nLet me actually run the script to get numbers right.\n\nAlso compute quantization overhead: per-group scale (group 128) weight overhead = 2/128 = 1.56%.\n\nAnd activation quantization overhead: reading FP16 activations, writing INT4, plus per-group scales/zero-points; in prefill, activation traffic dominates → W4A4 does NOT reduce prefill traffic much (activations are still read as FP16 into the quant kernel) → analytic reason why prefill gain must come from compute (INT4 TC) not bandwidth.\n\nLet me write and run.\n\nI'll also compute an estimated GPU-hour budget for the design (that's a resource estimate, allowed, with assumptions flagged).\n\nLet me do it.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"command": "mkdir -p /tmp/dry && cat > /tmp/dry/an.py <<'PY'\nimport math\nM={ # public LLaMA-2 architectural constants (ASSUMED from public configs; no local config present)\n 7B:=(4096,32,32,32,11008,32000),13B:=(5120,40,40,40,13824,32000),70B:=(8192,80,64,8,28672,32000)}\nHW={'A100-80G':dict(bw=2.039e12,fp16=312e12,int4=624e12,int8=624e12,has_int4_tc=True),\n    'H100-80G':dict(bw=3.352e12,fp16=989e12,int4=1979e12,int8=1979e12,has_int4_tc=False)}\ndef params(h,L,th,kvh,i,V):\n    return dict(emb=V*h, layers=L*(4*h*h+3*h*i), other=2*h)\ndef kv_per_tok(h,L,th,kvh):\n    hd=h//th; return 2*L*kvh*hd   # elements (K and V)\ndef wbytes(bits,g=None): # per-element bytes incl. group scale/zp overhead\n    b=bits/8.0\n    if g: b+= (16+16)/g/8.0*1.0   # fp16 scale+zero per group of g weights\n    return b\nprint(\"model  non-emb-params(B)  FP16-GB  W4A4w-GB  W8A8-GB | KV fp16 KB/tok  KV int4 KB/tok | W4A4(GB)+KV4096(GB)\")\nfor n,(h,L,th,kvh,i,V) in M.items():\n    p=params(h,L,th,kvh,i,V); ne=p['layers']/1e9\n    f16=p['emb']*2+p['layers']*2; w4=p['emb']*2+p['layers']*wbytes(4,128); w8=p['emb']*2+p['layers']*1.0\n    k=kv_per_tok(h,L,th,kvh)*2/1024; k4=kv_per_tok(h,L,th,kvh)*0.5/1024\n    print(f\"{n:5} {ne:8.2f}  {f16/2**30:7.1f} {w4/2**30:7.2f} {w8/2**30:7.1f} | {k:8.1f} {k4:8.1f} | {w4/2**30:6.2f}+{k4*4096/2**20:5.2f}\")\nprint()\nprint(\"Roofline crossover token-count M* (memory->compute bound) per regime; AI=2M/bytes_w approx\")\nfor hn,hw in HW.items():\n    for label,bits in [('FP16',16),('W8',8),('W4',4)]:\n        bw_el=wbytes(bits,128 if bits<16 else None)\n        peak = hw['fp16'] if bits==16 else (hw['int4'] if bits==4 else hw['int8'])\n        if bits==4 and not hw['has_int4_tc']: peak=hw['int8']\n        Mstar=(peak/hw['bw'])*bw_el/2\n        print(f\"  {hn} {label:5} bytes/elem={bw_el:.3f} ridge={peak/hw['bw']:6.1f} flop/B  M*={Mstar:7.1f} tokens\")\nprint()\nprint(\"Theoretical (overhead-free) speedup ceilings W4A4 vs FP16\")\nfor hn,hw in HW.items():\n    p4=hw['int4'] if hw['has_int4_tc'] else hw['int8']\n    print(f\"  {hn}: compute-bound ceil={p4/hw['fp16']:.2f}x  mem-bound weight-byte ceil={16/4:.1f}x (w/ scales {2/wbytes(4,128):.2f}x)\")\nprint()\nprint(\"Decode bytes-moved/token composition (weights + B*S*KV), analytic; ratio=decode traffic vs FP16\")\nfor n,(h,L,th,kvh,i,V) in M.items():\n    p=params(h,L,th,kvh,i,V)\n    for (B,S) in [(1,128),(1,4096),(8,4096),(64,4096)]:\n        wA=p['emb']*2+p['layers']*2; wB=p['emb']*2+p['layers']*wbytes(4,128)\n        kv=kv_per_tok(h,L,th,kvh); kA=B*S*kv*2; kB=B*S*kv*0.5\n        print(f\"  {n:4} B={B:2} S={S:4}: fp16={(wA+kA)/2**30:6.2f}GB w4a4={(wB+kB)/2**30:6.2f}GB traffic ratio={(wA+kA)/(wB+kB):5.2f}x  KVshare_fp16={100*kA/(wA+kA):4.1f}%\")\nprint()\nprint(\"Online-Hadamard analytic overhead per token per layer (fp16 activations, group=128)\")\nfor n,(h,L,th,kvh,i,V) in M.items():\n    flop_layer=4*h*h+3*h*i\n    for name,wd,bit in [('down_proj in (ffn dim)',i,16),('attn out / V (h)',h,16)]:\n        f=wd*math.log2(wd); bytes_rw=2*wd*bit/8\n        print(f\"  {n:4} {name:24} rotFLOP={f/1e3:7.1f}k ({100*f/flop_layer:5.3f}% of layer FLOP)  extra traffic={bytes_rw/1024:6.1f}KB/tok\")\n    # periodic KV-cache full-cache Hadamard: O(S * h * log h) per layer per refresh\n    print(f\"  {n:4} full-KV-refresh @S=4096 (per layer, fp16): {4096*h*math.log2(h)*L/1e9:8.2f} GFLOP total across {L} layers\")\nPY\npython3 /tmp/dry/an.py", "timeout_seconds": 60, "kind": "ExecuteCheckAction"}, "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-95735787ae15be72", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-95735787ae15be72", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "execute_check", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"mkdir -p /tmp/dry && cat > /tmp/dry/an.py <<'PY'\\nimport math\\nM={ # public LLaMA-2 architectural constants (ASSUMED from public configs; no local config present)\\n 7B:=(4096,32,32,32,11008,32000),13B:=(5120,40,40,40,13824,32000),70B:=(8192,80,64,8,28672,32000)}\\nHW={'A100-80G':dict(bw=2.039e12,fp16=312e12,int4=624e12,int8=624e12,has_int4_tc=True),\\n    'H100-80G':dict(bw=3.352e12,fp16=989e12,int4=1979e12,int8=1979e12,has_int4_tc=False)}\\ndef params(h,L,th,kvh,i,V):\\n    return dict(emb=V*h, layers=L*(4*h*h+3*h*i), other=2*h)\\ndef kv_per_tok(h,L,th,kvh):\\n    hd=h//th; return 2*L*kvh*hd   # elements (K and V)\\ndef wbytes(bits,g=None): # per-element bytes incl. group scale/zp overhead\\n    b=bits/8.0\\n    if g: b+= (16+16)/g/8.0*1.0   # fp16 scale+zero per group of g weights\\n    return b\\nprint(\\\"model  non-emb-params(B)  FP16-GB  W4A4w-GB  W8A8-GB | KV fp16 KB/tok  KV int4 KB/tok | W4A4(GB)+KV4096(GB)\\\")\\nfor n,(h,L,th,kvh,i,V) in M.items():\\n    p=params(h,L,th,kvh,i,V); ne=p['layers']/1e9\\n    f16=p['emb']*2+p['layers']*2; w4=p['emb']*2+p['layers']*wbytes(4,128); w8=p['emb']*2+p['layers']*1.0\\n    k=kv_per_tok(h,L,th,kv